[agent] Now I understand the workflow. I need to:
[agent] 1. Create feature groups for each data source (transactions, profiles, activity, account_health, transactions_late)
[agent] 2. Insert data into them
[agent] 3. Create a feature view that joins them
[agent] 4. Create a training dataset from the feature view
[agent] But wait - the task says to produce a training dataset with specific columns. The labels.csv has the label_time and churned. I need to think about this differently.
[agent] Looking at the schema:
[agent] - transactions.csv: account_id, event_time, amount, balance
[agent] - profiles.csv: account_id, event_time, credit_score, tier
[agent] - activity.csv: account_id, event_time, sessions_7d
[agent] - account_health.csv: account_id, event_time, health_score
[agent] - transactions_late.csv: account_id, event_time, amount, balance (same schema as transactions)
[agent] - labels.csv: account_id, label_time, churned
[agent] The training dataset needs: account_id, label_time, amount, balance, credit_score, tier, sessions_7d, health_score, churned
[agent] For each (account_id, label_time) in labels.csv, I need the MOST RECENT value from each source table at or before label_time.
[agent] This is a point-in-time join problem. The feature view should handle this with the event_time and label_time.
[agent] Let me first create feature groups for each source, then a feature view, then compute the training dataset.
